\caption(The panels use different vertical scales so all three families remain visible. These are logical comparisons, excluding preprocessing, rather than timing measurements or a random-text benchmark.)
\alttext(Comparisons per text byte grow approximately with pattern length for repeated full matches. Unit-shift mismatches stay near one, while absent-byte skips decrease toward zero.)

> Boundary and byte controls

The trace exposes the raw negative bad-character proposal when it occurs.
For AABB against ABAB, the final B matches and the next B mismatches A at
pattern index two. The rightmost pattern B is at index three, hence bad=-1.
The strong good-suffix rule supplies four, ensuring safe forward progress.
The sentinel for a full-match mismatch index is m, not a valid pattern index.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  struct Example {std::string name,text,pattern;};
  const std::vector<Example> examples{
      {"overlapping matches","aaaa","aa"},{"empty pattern","abc",""},
      {"pattern longer than text","ab","abc"},{"case-sensitive","ABCabc","abc"},
      {"embedded NUL",std::string("A\0B\0B",5),std::string("\0B",2)},
      {"high bytes",std::string("\xff\x80\xff",3),std::string("\xff",1)},
      {"negative raw bad shift","AABB","ABAB"}};
  std::print("| case | text bytes | pattern bytes | match starts | visited alignments | comparisons |\n"
             "| :--- | ---: | ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (const auto& example:examples) {
    const auto trace=dm::algorithms::boyer_moore_trace(example.text,example.pattern);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",example.name,trace.text_size,trace.pattern_size,
        trace.matches,trace.alignments.size(),trace.comparisons);
  }
  const auto trace=dm::algorithms::boyer_moore_trace("AABB","ABAB");const auto& step=trace.alignments.front();
  std::print("\nNegative-shift control: raw bad {}, good {}, chosen {}.\n",
      step.bad_character_shift,step.good_suffix_shift,step.shift);
}
```
